{
  "supported": true,
  "title": "S4 draft independent acceptance - Tank Rescue",
  "development_plan": [
    "Independent reviewer uses this plan only after autonomous game generation has ended; never provide it to generation or repair."
  ],
  "state_contract": {
    "water": "Actual stored water, integer 0..5",
    "moves": "Actual remaining moves, integer 0..4",
    "delivered": "Actual deliveries, integer 0..2",
    "phase": "Actual Playing, Won or Lost"
  },
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "text": "Initially water=2, moves=4, delivered=0 and phase=Playing. Water capacity is 5; the goal is 2 deliveries.",
      "verification": "automated"
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "text": "While Playing, Pump adds 3 water capped at 5 and consumes exactly 1 move, even when the tank was already full.",
      "verification": "automated"
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "text": "While Playing with water below 4, Deliver is a complete no-op: water, moves, delivered and phase all remain unchanged.",
      "verification": "automated"
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "text": "While Playing with water at least 4, Deliver consumes exactly 4 water and 1 move and adds exactly 1 delivery.",
      "verification": "automated"
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "text": "After each move-consuming action, check the delivery goal first: delivered=2 means Won; otherwise moves=0 means Lost; otherwise stay Playing. Winning on the final move is Won, not Lost.",
      "verification": "automated"
    },
    {
      "id": "R6",
      "text": "In Won or Lost, Pump and Deliver must not change any value. They may remain enabled and ignore activation, or be disabled.",
      "verification": "manual"
    },
    {
      "id": "R7",
      "text": "Restart is always enabled and immediately restores all four initial values in every phase, including after an invalid action.",
      "verification": "automated"
    },
    {
      "id": "R8",
      "text": "Show short English instructions explaining the initial resources, water capacity, Pump cost at the cap, Deliver cost, insufficient-water no-op, delivery goal, move exhaustion, win-before-loss priority, terminal lock and Restart. Give each button an understandable accessible name.",
      "verification": "manual"
    },
    {
      "id": "R9",
      "text": "Use native buttons #pump, #deliver and #restart. The visible #water, #moves and #delivered contain bare integers, and #phase contains exactly Playing, Won or Lost. Mark a visible game area with data-game-surface. Expose window.__gameTest.getState() as a fresh read-only snapshot of actual water, moves, delivered and phase; provide no state setters.",
      "verification": "automated"
    }
  ],
